// CreateAgentAccountSignupWithBody Start a headless, payment-first account signup
//
// Opens a hosted Stripe Checkout Session for a payment-first, headless account signup. No account and no session cookie exist yet: complete checkout_url with your own browser automation, then claim the account with claim_secret at POST /v1/agent/accounts/{signup_id}/claim. Every field is validated before any Stripe call, followed by the same restricted-jurisdiction and allowlist gates the human signup paths apply. accept_terms_version must equal the server's current policy version, returned in the policy_version_stale error when it does not match. pack selects a minute pack by id; amount and currency come back server derived and must never be sent in the request. data_region is derived from your network location and an optional hint is honored only when it agrees with that derivation. signup_id is region-prefixed (hsr1:<region>:<id>) and must be presented back verbatim to the claim route, so the request reaches the same regional backend that holds the row. Set dry_run to true to validate the request and get back a synthetic 200 response with no Stripe session created and no charge possible, for rehearsing the shape before spending real money; a dry run signup_id is never region-prefixed and can never be claimed.
